# Clock Sync — Use `getAdjustedNow()`

Clients sync to server time via the `get_server_time_ms` RPC: 8 samples, keep
the 4 with lowest RTT, use the **median offset** (see
`src/data/supabase/server-time.ts`). Offset is refreshed every 60s.

**Anywhere timer state is computed or written, use `getAdjustedNow()`** instead
of `Date.now()`. The drift between two browsers can be hundreds of ms — using
`Date.now()` on the client makes timers visibly desync.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — uses raw client clock
const startTimestamp = Date.now();

// ✅ GOOD — server-aligned
import { getAdjustedNow } from '../data/supabase/server-time';
const startTimestamp = getAdjustedNow();
```

`Date.now()` is fine for non-timer concerns (logging, throttling, UI animation
timestamps that don't affect synced state).
